//RS // D-IO-PROMPT1=A: one prompt reader for every tier. A read that returns no
//RS // bytes means the stream is closed and will never answer again, which is a
//RS // different fact from an answer this kernel can reject and ask about a second
//RS // time. Only a rejected answer may re-prompt. Engines marshal this outcome;
//RS // they never re-derive it, so no engine can spin where another one stops.
